/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ A tiny "library" script meant to be imported, not run directly. `\i` (at
/ the prompt or nested in a script — see examples/README.md) runs a script like `\l`, then moves every
/ table/global/function it newly bound at its top level under `.namespace_lib.*`
/ (the file's stem), so it doesn't collide with names already in the session.
/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

double: {[x] x*2}
greeting: "hello from namespace_lib"
lookup: select sym, price from trades where price > 100
